1
00:00:06,519 --> 00:00:10,160
Now I'm going to find the little princess.

2
00:00:10,919 --> 00:00:12,842
With my black box.

3
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:16,881
How does it work?

4
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:26,805
Norman, how does this work?

5
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:30,489
Well, you put that bit in the water.

6
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:35,006
Then you pull the handle. And the water goes in.

7
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:38,891
OK. There's water in it.

8
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:40,730
What do I do now?

9
00:00:41,119 --> 00:00:43,804
You push the handle in...

10
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,128
And the water comes out!

11
00:00:49,119 --> 00:00:52,089
Yes, it works like that.

12
00:00:59,679 --> 00:01:02,159
How does this work, Corvax?

13
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:05,810
You press this switch and...

14
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:09,361
the doors go up.

15
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:12,525
Now you press the other switch...

16
00:01:12,719 --> 00:01:13,719
and...

17
00:01:14,439 --> 00:01:16,806
The doors come down.

18
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:19,883
Yes, Thimbo.

19
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:22,725
And no one can get in.

20
00:01:23,519 --> 00:01:25,965
Now, the windows...

21
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:28,523
Go up...

22
00:01:32,480 --> 00:01:35,130
And down!

23
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:40,570
And no one can see us.

24
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:42,206
That's right.

25
00:01:43,079 --> 00:01:44,603
What are these?

26
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,571
They're for the video.

27
00:01:48,599 --> 00:01:52,001
This one turns the video on.

28
00:01:57,280 --> 00:02:00,602
And this one turns it off.

29
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:03,569
What does it do?

30
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:05,560
Look!

31
00:02:05,799 --> 00:02:09,770
Those pictures are coming from outside.

32
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:13,050
Wow! That's clever!

33
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:15,846
I am clever.

34
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:23,807
Oh dear! The baby needs some food.

35
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,128
What are we going to do?

36
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:45,323
One. Put some milk in a bottle.

37
00:02:47,639 --> 00:02:50,369
Pour the milk into the bottle, Thimbo!

38
00:02:50,759 --> 00:02:52,887
I am pouring it.

39
00:02:53,159 --> 00:02:55,320
That's too much.

40
00:02:56,639 --> 00:02:58,288
It's cold.

41
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,322
Two. Warm the milk.

42
00:03:03,719 --> 00:03:04,924
How?

43
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:07,368
Put it there!

44
00:03:16,159 --> 00:03:19,129
That's better. It's warmer now.

45
00:03:21,599 --> 00:03:23,920
I'm going to give it to the baby.

46
00:03:24,599 --> 00:03:25,760
Put this on.

47
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:33,884
No! On the bottle!

48
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,080
There!

49
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:39,727
Nice baby!

50
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:44,527
You're going to have a nice drink.

51
00:03:44,719 --> 00:03:46,880
Not nice! Not nice!

52
00:03:48,759 --> 00:03:49,805
Nice!

53
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:51,730
Nice!

54
00:03:54,039 --> 00:03:57,122
All right. Here, Thimbo.

55
00:03:57,319 --> 00:03:58,843
You do it!

56
00:04:10,759 --> 00:04:12,408
Can you see anything?

57
00:04:12,599 --> 00:04:14,089
Can you see Amanda?

58
00:04:15,719 --> 00:04:17,049
Wait!

59
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,650
Ah! Yes! Yes!

60
00:04:21,839 --> 00:04:23,409
I can see her now.

61
00:04:23,639 --> 00:04:25,004
What's she doing?

62
00:04:25,199 --> 00:04:26,848
She's having a drink.

63
00:04:27,279 --> 00:04:29,407
She's drinking from a bottle.

64
00:04:29,879 --> 00:04:31,290
Where is she?

65
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:34,608
I can see a house.

66
00:04:34,959 --> 00:04:36,039
What's it like?

67
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:49,481
I've got something for you.

68
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:51,125
What is it?

69
00:04:51,319 --> 00:04:52,764
It's a present.

70
00:04:52,959 --> 00:04:54,199
What's it like?

71
00:04:54,399 --> 00:04:57,084
It's big. Very big.

72
00:04:57,279 --> 00:04:58,565
Is it heavy?

73
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:02,609
Oh, yes. It's very heavy.

74
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:04,884
What color is it?

75
00:05:05,079 --> 00:05:06,843
Black and white.

76
00:05:07,399 --> 00:05:08,685
Is it an animal?

77
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:11,963
Yes, it is. It's an animal.

78
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:14,005
What kind of animal is it?

79
00:05:16,079 --> 00:05:17,444
It's a cat!

80
00:05:17,959 --> 00:05:20,530
Come back! Come back!

81
00:05:25,319 --> 00:05:26,764
What's it like?

82
00:05:27,319 --> 00:05:29,605
It's a very small house.

83
00:05:31,079 --> 00:05:33,127
It's got a blue door.

84
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:35,881
And it's got three windows.

85
00:05:36,319 --> 00:05:37,843
And where is the house?

86
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:40,165
Oh!

87
00:05:41,839 --> 00:05:45,638
There are rocks... big rocks.

88
00:05:47,759 --> 00:05:50,729
The house is behind the rocks.

89
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:53,090
How far is it?

90
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:58,409
The black box says it's twenty kilometres from here.

91
00:06:01,439 --> 00:06:02,929
How do we get there?

92
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:04,646
Which way do we go?

93
00:06:04,879 --> 00:06:06,608
North? South?

94
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:09,200
East? West?

95
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:18,404
Going North...

96
00:06:19,399 --> 00:06:21,128
Going South...

97
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:24,129
Going East...

98
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:26,690
Going West.

99
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:30,361
Some people go by train.

100
00:06:33,839 --> 00:06:36,160
Some people go by plane.

101
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:42,006
Some people go by car.

102
00:06:45,439 --> 00:06:48,841
But I like my bike.

103
00:06:54,079 --> 00:06:56,320
Some people go by bus.

104
00:07:00,199 --> 00:07:02,280
Some people go by boat.

105
00:07:05,879 --> 00:07:09,166
Some people go by spaceship.

106
00:07:14,319 --> 00:07:18,448
But I like my bike.

107
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:29,601
All right! We can go by car.

108
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:32,041
Which way do we go, Muzzy?

109
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:35,768
I don't know.

110
00:07:35,959 --> 00:07:39,121
-The box isn't working -It doesn't matter.

111
00:07:39,319 --> 00:07:41,048
We can ask someone. Come on!

112
00:07:47,399 --> 00:07:48,810
Now!

113
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,321
You're going to have a lesson.

114
00:07:53,519 --> 00:07:56,648
You're going to learn some words.

115
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:59,765
And the first word is...

116
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:02,641
Corvax.

117
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:06,801
Cor-vax.

118
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,001
Cor-vax.

119
00:08:10,519 --> 00:08:14,001
-Don't laugh! It isn't funny. -It is.

120
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:19,401
Say "Cor-vax".

121
00:08:21,040 --> 00:08:25,283
Cor -Cor -Cor -

122
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:28,126
Cor -Cor -Cor -

123
00:08:28,439 --> 00:08:31,522
Shut up, Thimbo! This is not a joke.

124
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:35,087
She isn't going to say it. She doesn't understand you.

125
00:08:35,279 --> 00:08:37,850
And you don't understand anything.

126
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:43,202
Now, go over there and look outside.

127
00:08:45,679 --> 00:08:49,763
Now say "Corvax is..."

128
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,450
Silly! Silly!

129
00:08:51,639 --> 00:08:53,163
No! No! Say

130
00:08:53,399 --> 00:08:56,209
"Corvax is going to be

131
00:08:56,440 --> 00:08:59,602
the King of Gondoland".

132
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:04,851
-Corvax is... -Good!

133
00:09:05,039 --> 00:09:07,519
That's good! Say it again!

134
00:09:08,039 --> 00:09:11,760
Corvax is...

135
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:14,566
Yes, yes.

136
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:20,529
...going to be... wet! Wet!

137
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:23,563
-Wet! -Naughty little girl!

138
00:09:23,919 --> 00:09:27,081
Say "Corvax is going to be

139
00:09:27,279 --> 00:09:30,089
the King of Gondoland".

140
00:09:30,679 --> 00:09:34,603
Now, are you going to say it properly?

141
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:37,841
No. Not going to.

142
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:55,564
Excuse me.

143
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:58,088
Yes? Can I help you?

144
00:09:58,279 --> 00:09:59,519
Yes, please.

145
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:02,803
We're looking for a place with big rocks, and...

146
00:10:03,039 --> 00:10:05,485
Oh, there are lots of places like that near here.

147
00:10:06,399 --> 00:10:08,720
We're looking for a very small house.

148
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:12,961
Avery small house. Do you understand?

149
00:10:13,639 --> 00:10:17,166
Oh yes. I understand.

150
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:20,931
A small house.

151
00:10:22,879 --> 00:10:24,802
What's it like?

152
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:28,124
It's got a blue door, and three windows.

153
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:30,720
It's behind some rocks.

154
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:36,963
There is a house like that near here.

155
00:10:38,519 --> 00:10:41,728
Who lives there? Who lives in the house?

156
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:44,241
No one lives there.

157
00:10:45,159 --> 00:10:47,445
But there is someone...

158
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:52,561
He doesn't live there.

159
00:10:52,759 --> 00:10:56,241
But he sometimes goes there.

160
00:10:56,720 --> 00:10:58,324
What's he like?

161
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,605
He's tall,

162
00:11:02,039 --> 00:11:05,930
and he walks like this.

163
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:13,611
He's got a green face and a long nose.

164
00:11:14,399 --> 00:11:17,049
And he wears funny hats.

165
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:19,806
That's Corvax.

166
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:25,170
He's got a green face.

167
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:28,170
He's got a long nose.

168
00:11:28,679 --> 00:11:30,602
He wears funny hats.

169
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:32,884
He's very tall.

170
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:36,161
And he walks like this.

171
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:39,328
<i>That's Corvax!</i>

172
00:11:55,159 --> 00:11:56,364
Here we are!

173
00:11:56,559 --> 00:11:58,765
Look! We can get through there.

174
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:00,121
Come on!

175
00:12:01,799 --> 00:12:03,164
Oh dear!

176
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:05,931
I can't get through.

177
00:12:07,159 --> 00:12:09,526
It isn't wide enough.

178
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:14,207
I'm too fat.

179
00:12:14,399 --> 00:12:16,367
It's wider up there.

180
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:19,401
Muzzy! You're the biggest.

181
00:12:19,639 --> 00:12:22,404
Lift the Queen up! Carry her through!

182
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:25,886
Oh! Muzzy!

183
00:12:26,279 --> 00:12:30,442
Thank you. Thank you so much!

184
00:12:30,679 --> 00:12:33,329
Go on, Muzzy! That's the widest pan.

185
00:12:33,559 --> 00:12:34,764
Up there!

186
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:40,445
Wide.

187
00:12:43,039 --> 00:12:44,484
Wider.

188
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:48,050
Widest.

189
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:54,286
Big.

190
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:57,050
Bigger.

191
00:12:58,320 --> 00:12:59,810
Biggest.

192
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:04,283
My hat's big.

193
00:13:04,519 --> 00:13:06,043
My hat's bigger.

194
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:08,004
His hat's the biggest,

195
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:10,201
but he can't see anything.

196
00:13:11,799 --> 00:13:13,129
Fast

197
00:13:14,159 --> 00:13:15,570
Faster.

198
00:13:17,039 --> 00:13:18,609
Fastest.

199
00:13:23,720 --> 00:13:25,290
I'm fast.

200
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:27,209
I' m faster.

201
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:31,208
He's the fastest.

202
00:13:33,919 --> 00:13:35,330
Good.

203
00:13:37,240 --> 00:13:38,526
Better.

204
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:41,731
Best.

205
00:13:47,399 --> 00:13:48,969
This is good.

206
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:52,970
This is better.

207
00:13:55,799 --> 00:13:57,642
This is the best.

208
00:14:19,639 --> 00:14:21,129
The King's coming.

209
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:24,085
With the others -Bob, Sylvia -

210
00:14:24,399 --> 00:14:27,289
-Where's the baby? -She's over there.

211
00:14:29,279 --> 00:14:32,646
No, she isn't. Where is she?

212
00:14:34,639 --> 00:14:36,800
She's got my box!

213
00:14:37,399 --> 00:14:39,163
She's invisible!

214
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:42,321
What are we going to do?

215
00:14:42,519 --> 00:14:45,204
We're going to find her.

216
00:14:45,399 --> 00:14:46,923
Where's your box?

217
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:50,043
I haven't got it. It's in the river.

218
00:14:51,039 --> 00:14:53,360
Now there's only one box,

219
00:14:53,559 --> 00:14:55,959
and she's got it!

